  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964559/assets/e589960ec2647179ac013cf60286129ece1d31e5daa8bf16fdeb237e942c92df.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The helicopter's pilot represents the three locations in vector form, as shown in the diagram. Taking the helipad as the origin, find the coordinates of the position vectors $p,$ $q,$ and $r$ of the points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R,$ respectively.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $p=\u27e8$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,0,\\,3\u27e9\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $q=\u27e80,\\,-3,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\u27e9\\,,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r=\u27e80,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,3\u27e9\\,.$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that in general, if a point $A$ has coordinates $({a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}),$ then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OA}=\u27e8{a}_{x},{a}_{y},{a}_{z}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nHere, the point $P$ has coordinates $(0,0,3),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e80,0,3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe point $Q$ has coordinates $(0,-3,2),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =\u27e80,-3,2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe point $R$ has coordinates $(0,4,3),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\u27e80,4,3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
